      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/p/858c86/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2012-09-27T08:40:03.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>So, played my first game with Unity. She's a lot of fun, but I had a question on how her golems work with damage buffs. For example, when agent adept plays his song to add 1 dmg to a target, each golem would count&nbsp;as a target, correct? I can't add that dmg to unity and up all the golems' dmg because they're dealing it, not her. If I wanted to up their&nbsp;dmg, I would have to choose two of them. That makes the most sense to keep her balance. How does that work with someone like Legacy who just does a blanket +1 to all heroes? I'm guess it just doesn't apply to golems, correct? Instead, it would only apply to her cards that say, \"Unity deals....\" Does she just not really synergize well with Legacy then?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:36:15.527Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
